    "innovation": "This paper provides robust evidence for upper-ocean warming from 1993-2008 by compiling, reprocessing, and performing a detailed error analysis on inconsistent historical data sets to resolve previous discrepancies and quantify uncertainties.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Argo profiling float system",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "temperature",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "The revolution has been brought about by two major developments. The first is millimetre-precision altimetry from satellites to give sea level globally since 1992; the second is the Argo profiling float system of nominally 3,000 floats that provide vertical profiles of temperature and salinity over the upper 2,000 metres of the ocean every 10 days or so.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Argo profiling float system",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "salinity",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "The revolution has been brought about by two major developments. The first is millimetre-precision altimetry from satellites to give sea level globally since 1992; the second is the Argo profiling float system of nominally 3,000 floats that provide vertical profiles of temperature and salinity over the upper 2,000 metres of the ocean every 10 days or so.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "expendable bathythermographs (XBTs)",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "temperatures",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Before then, the bulk of the observations of the ocean were from expendable bathythermographs (XBTs) dropped from ships along their tracks as opportunities arose. As a result, coverage was spotty and irregular, and missing over many regions such as the Southern Ocean. The XBTs recorded temperatures, but their depths were estimated on the basis of an assigned drop rate, which turned out to be sensitive to the exact design and character of the XBT probe.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "expendable bathythermographs (XBTs)",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MOUNTED_ON",
            "target_entity_instance": "ships",
            "target_entity_type": "Platform",
            "paragraph": "Before then, the bulk of the observations of the ocean were from expendable bathythermographs (XBTs) dropped from ships along their tracks as opportunities arose.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "altimetry",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MOUNTED_ON",
            "target_entity_instance": "satellites",
            "target_entity_type": "Platform",
            "paragraph": "The revolution has been brought about by two major developments. The first is millimetre-precision altimetry from satellites to give sea level globally since 1992; the second is the Argo profiling float system of nominally 3,000 floats that provide vertical profiles of temperature and salinity over the upper 2,000 metres of the ocean every 10 days or so.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Lyman et al. analysis of the global upper ocean from 1993 to 2008",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "average warming of 0.64 \u00b1 0.29 watts per square metre",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "In spite of all the difficulties, Lyman et al. are able to demonstrate a robust warming of the global upper ocean from 1993 to 2008, depicted by the red line in Figure 1, which averages 0.64 \u00b1 0.29 watts per square metre (95% confidence interval) for the Earth as a whole.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "independent analysis of the full-depth Argo floats for 2003 to 2008",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "6-year heat-content increase of 0.77 \u00b10.11 W m\u00b2 for the global ocean",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "However, independent analysis of the full-depth Argo floats for 2003 to 2008 suggests that the 6-year heat-content increase is 0.77 \u00b10.11 W m\u00b2 for the global ocean or 0.54 W m\u00b2 for the entire Earth, indicating that substantial warming may be taking place below the upper 700 m (Fig. 1, blue line).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        }
